// The payload: one long stream cut into 64 KiB chunks, each authenticated on its
// own.
//
// https://age-encryption.org/v1 (the STREAM construction, of Hoang, Reyhanitabar,
// Rogaway and Vizár)
//
// Chunking is what lets a file be sealed and opened without being held whole:
// the sender encrypts a chunk, writes it, and forgets it. The price is that the
// chunk index has to be authenticated along with the data — otherwise a chunk
// could be dropped, repeated or moved — which is what the last two bytes of every
// nonce are for.
//
// Not here: reading and writing. This turns 64 KiB of plaintext into 64 KiB and a
// tag, and back; where those bytes come from and go to is the caller's business.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moonseal/internal/crypt",
  "moonbitstack/moonseal/spec",
}

import {
  "moonbitlang/core/buffer",
} for "test"
